        "original_id": "7153c282-1c4f-5214-9be8-15c9b99548f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Užupis, Freetown Christiania, Belmontas, Rasos, Copenhagen, Paris\n- People: Christian Skeel\n- Concepts: bohemian atmosphere, laissez-faire atmosphere\n\nFacts:\n- Užupis has long been popular with artists.\n- Užupis has been compared to Montmartre in Paris and to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen because of its bohemian and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- In April 2011, residents of Freetown Christiania temporarily closed it while discussions with the Danish government about its future continued.\n- After the April 2011 closure, Freetown Christiania re-opened to the public.\n- Belmontas is located in the area of Rasos on the right bank of the Vilnia River, east of Užupis.\n- Christian Skeel lives and works in Copenhagen.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d624c3c9-997a-5f55-94fd-13e84441842d",
        "text": "Page: Užupis. Sentence: The district has been popular with artists for some time, and has been compared to Montmartre in Paris and to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen, due to its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\nPage: Freetown Christiania. Sentence: It was temporarily closed by residents in April 2011 while discussions continued with the Danish government about its future, but then re-opened to the public.\nPage: Belmontas. Sentence: It is located in the area of Rasos, on the right bank of Vilnia River, to the east of Užupis.\nPage: Christian Skeel. Sentence: He lives and works in Copenhagen.",
